H…7}š»¥@*ÁªÛëFµÅŒ×Ø‘±ÎÚÔ'Š¤~±{"url":"/gcsl/tools/checking-and-formatting/","fragment":{"page_number":0,"data":{"url":"/gcsl/tools/checking-and-formatting/","content":"Checking and Formatting Programs. You can check a GCSL program without running its effects, then format its source consistently. The checker and formatter deliberately have different scopes: checking needs workspace relationships; formatting only needs source text that parses. Before you start # You need gcsl and an existing source file or workspace. Commit or save your changes before rewriting files so you can review the formatting diff. Check and format # Check a file, including its enclosing workspace if it has one: Copygcsl check main.gcsl Preview whether formatting would change that file: Copygcsl fmt --check main.gcsl Apply the formatter and repeat the check: Copygcsl fmt main.gcsl gcsl fmt --check main.gcsl Check the result # The checker reports its summary on standard error. Warnings alone do not make it fail. The final formatting check succeeds without listing the file when it is already formatted. A file with lexical or syntax errors is left untouched by the formatter; fix those diagnostics and retry. Formatting does not require a successful type check. It uses one language style rather than editor-specific indent settings. Checking a tree # With no paths, both commands use the enclosing workspace and exclude nested workspaces. An explicit directory makes them discover nested workspaces too. However, gcsl check DIRECTORY checks workspaces, not unattached .gcsl files under that directory. Pass each standalone file explicitly when it also needs checking. For automation, gcsl check --message-format json main.gcsl writes one JSON diagnostic per line to standard output and keeps the summary on standard error. See gcsl(1) for the schema and exit statuses.","word_count":259,"filters":{},"meta":{"crumbs":"GCSL / Development Tools","title":"Checking and Formatting Programs"},"anchors":[{"element":"h2","id":"before-you-start","text":"Before you start #","location":38},{"element":"h2","id":"check-and-format","text":"Check and format #","location":67},{"element":"h2","id":"check-the-result","text":"Check the result #","location":110},{"element":"h2","id":"checking-a-tree","text":"Checking a tree #","location":179}]}},"word_data":{"effect":[{"position":13,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"copygcsl":[{"position":82,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":92,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":103,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"howev":[{"position":205,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"schema":[{"position":255,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"no":[{"position":184,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"then":[{"position":14,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"fmt":[{"position":93,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":104,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":107,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"checker":[{"position":20,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":115,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"success":[{"position":166,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"directori":[{"position":198,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":208,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":217,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"standard":[{"position":120,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":242,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":249,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"editorspecif":[{"position":176,"weight":24,"original_word":null}],"gcsl":[{"position":8,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":44,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":84,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":95,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":105,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":106,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":109,"weight":12,"original_word":null},{"position":206,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":213,"weight":24,"original_word":null},{"position":230,"weight":24,"o